<Layout title="Healthcare for your college student | Kin & Campus" description="A local board-certified pediatrician helps college students in Blacksburg continue medications, address illnesses, complete forms, and learn to manage their health.">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">For parents</div><h1>Keep their healthcare steady while they are away at college.</h1><p class="lead">Kin &amp; Campus gives your student an established physician in Blacksburg who can coordinate ongoing care throughout the academic year. The program supports the medical needs they already have while helping them become more capable participants in their own care.</p></div>
<div class="w"><img class="photo" src={href("photos/arch-fall.jpg")} width="678" height="452" alt="A stone arch on campus under fall trees">

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:48px">Before the school year</div>
<h2>Put the important pieces in place before they are needed.</h2>
<p class="lead">An introductory conversation can identify what should be transferred, documented, or scheduled before classes begin. The details vary by student, but these are common priorities.</p>
<ol class="steps">
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div><h3>Establish local care</h3><p>A first visit gives the physician and student time to review the existing plan before a refill is due or an illness interrupts the week.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div><h3>Plan for ongoing prescriptions</h3><p>ADHD medication and anxiety or depression medication often require regular follow-up. Asthma, allergy, and acne treatment also work better when someone is watching how the plan fits campus life.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div><h3>Complete university requirements</h3><p>Immunization documentation, sports physicals, and housing accommodations can require a clinician's review. Starting early leaves time to obtain the right records.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div><h3>Agree on communication</h3><p>Your student controls their medical information once they are an adult. We make communication preferences explicit so everyone understands when and how you may be included.</p></div></li>
</ol>
<p class="cite"><a href="https://www.healthychildren.org/English/ages-stages/young-adult/Pages/Healthy-Tips-for-the-College-Freshman.aspx">AAP college checklist</a>. <a href="https://healthcenter.vt.edu/new_student/required_immunizations.html">VT immunizations</a>. <a href="https://ssd.vt.edu/access/housing.html">VT SSD housing</a>.</p>

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">During the academic year</div>
<h2>Care continues as their schedule and needs change.</h2>
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>Medication management</h3><p>We follow established treatment, arrange appropriate refills, and discuss changes with the student. The hometown physician is updated when coordination is clinically appropriate.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Sick visits</h3><p>A physician who knows the student's baseline can evaluate common illnesses in context and help determine when a higher level of care is necessary.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Academic-year check-ins</h3><p>Move-in, the return from a break, and finals are useful times to review medication routines, symptoms, sleep, stress, and upcoming needs.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Growing independence</h3><p>Students practice making appointments, requesting refills, asking questions, and following a treatment plan while they still have structured support.</p></div>
</div>

<div style="margin-top:56px"><h2>Start with a straightforward conversation.</h2><p class="lead" style="margin-bottom:28px">We will explain the program, learn what kind of support your student may need, and decide whether Kin &amp; Campus is the right fit. Please save medical details for a secure clinical conversation rather than the website form.</p>
<p><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Request an introduction</a> &nbsp; <a class="lnk" href={href("membership")}>Learn how membership works &rarr;</a></p></div>
</div>
</Layout>
